# Check these out with LF on every platform.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is the Git for Windows default, so a Windows checkout would
# otherwise rewrite them to CRLF. That is not cosmetic here: Go test files embed
# bash scripts in raw string literals, and a stray \r ends up inside the script's
# arguments — `touch hook-ran.txt` starts creating a file whose name ends in a
# carriage return. The shell scripts under scripts/ and site/ are run by bash on
# Windows too, and break the same way.
*.go text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
